<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lubart</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1384</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Liubartas, Dmitry Lubart</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lubart was a son of Grand Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gediminas">Gediminas</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> who married into the princely house of Galicia-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volhynia">Volhynia</a> and became ruler of Volhynia after 1340. For decades he fought Casimir III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and Louis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> over the former Galician-Volhynian lands, keeping most of Volhynia. He built the brick castle at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutsk">Lutsk</a> that bears his name and ruled with the support of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> Ruthenian nobles.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lubart.jpg" alt="Lubart" width="283" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liubartas_King_Galicia-Volhynia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
